格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"将DeepSeek Harness插件列表按来源分组展示——官方插件与自行安装插件，一目了然。","id":"gh:1333885575","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-plugin-diraud","slug":"tttwh/dsh-plugin-diraud","topics":["deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","dsh","dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"将DeepSeek Harness插件列表按来源分组展示——官方插件与自行安装插件，一目了然。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-plugin-diraud"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A DeepSeek Harness (DSH)\nplugin-management enhancement: group the plugin list by source so you can t"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"ell\n**official** plugins apart from the ones **you installed yourself** at a glance."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Features"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- **`/plugin-audit` command**: lists the currently loaded plugins grouped by\nofficial / self-install"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ed, with `user` / `official` / keyword filtering;\n- **Self-installed plugin toggles (two surfaces)**"},{"id":"p6s3","text":":\n- Sidebar footer **Plugin Catalog** entry (icon button; click to open a\npanel): an enable/disable "},{"id":"p6s4","text":"**button** on every self-installed card;\n- Composer: `/plugin-audit disable|enable <keyword>`;\n- Bot"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"h persist to the profile's `cordis.patch.yml` (kept across restarts,\nreversible) and call `ctx.loade"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"r.update` for live effect (HMR-independent);\nofficial/builtin plugins are locked;\n- **Plugin Catalog"},{"id":"p6s7","text":" panel** (sidebar footer entry, since v0.5):\n- Cards grouped by source with a source badge, installe"},{"id":"p6s8","text":"d version, entry id\nand description; a search box filters by module name / entry id and every\nsectio"},{"id":"p6s9","text":"n shows a live count; a retry button appears if the list fails to\nload;\n- **Bilingual descriptions**"},{"id":"p6s10","text":" (v0.6): a built-in module-name → {zh, en}\ndictionary is consulted first so card descriptions follow"},{"id":"p6s11","text":" the UI language,\nfalling back to each package's own `description`;\n- **GitHub link** (v0.8): when a"},{"id":"p6s12","text":" package's `repository` / `homepage` points\nto GitHub, the card shows a GitHub button that opens its"},{"id":"p6s13","text":" full feature\ndocumentation (independent of the built-in \"Plugin list\" page);\n- **Self-installed plu"},{"id":"p6s14","text":"gin updates (v0.6)**:\n- The npm registry is checked automatically when the panel opens; the top\n\"Upd"},{"id":"p6s15","text":"ate\" bar shows how many plugins are outdated, with **Re-check** and\n**Update all** buttons, and ever"},{"id":"p6s16","text":"y registry-installed card has its own\n**Update** button plus a progress bar while running\n(`pnpm add"},{"id":"p6s17","text":" <pkg>@latest --config.minimumReleaseAge=0`, corepack/npx\nfallback, live output);\n- **GitHub plugin "},{"id":"p6s18","text":"updates (v0.9)**: plugins installed from `github:` / `git+`\n/ `git://` / `git@` specs can be updated"},{"id":"p6s19","text":" even without an npm package —\nbranch/default-branch refs compare the locally-locked commit against "},{"id":"p6s20","text":"the\nremote HEAD via `git ls-remote`, tag refs list all tags to find a newer\nstable tag; updates re-r"},{"id":"p6s21","text":"un `pnpm add <original spec>` (or the new tag spec);\nrefs pinned to a specific commit are marked not"},{"id":"p6s22","text":" auto-updatable;\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Screenshot"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Sidebar footer **Plugin Catalog** entry (since v0.5) — click to open the panel: self-installed plugi"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"ns grouped by origin, each card with an enable/disable toggle:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"The top bar shows the update area (`可更新: 1` = 1 update available, `重新检查`\n= re-check, `全部更新` = update"},{"id":"p9s2","text":" all), followed by the search box and the\ngrouped cards. Every card carries the enable/disable toggl"},{"id":"p9s3","text":"e, version, GitHub\nbutton, update status and uninstall button:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Quick start"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Prerequisites: `pnpm`, the `dsh` CLI."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"**Restart `dsh web`**, then:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"- Type `/plugin-audit` in the composer, or\n- Click the **Plugin Catalog** entry at the sidebar foote"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"Type `/plugin-audit` in the composer, or\n- Click the **Plugin Catalog** entry at the sidebar footer."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Commands"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| Command | Purpose |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| `/plugin-audit` | Overview: self-installed one-by-one + official count |\n| `/plugin-audit user` | "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"Self-installed only |\n| `/plugin-audit official` | Official only (full list) |\n| `/plugin-audit <key"},{"id":"p17s3","text":"word>` | Filter by package / entry keyword |\n| `/plugin-audit disable <keyword>` | Disable a matchin"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"g **self-installed** plugin (persisted) |\n| `/plugin-audit enable <keyword>` | Enable a matching **s"},{"id":"p17s5","text":"elf-installed** plugin (persisted) |\n| `dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-plugin-diraud` | Uninsta"},{"id":"p17s6","text":"installed** plugin (persisted) |\n| `dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-plugin-diraud` | Uninstall |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"> **How toggles persist**: `disable/enable` writes a `- id: <raw config id>` +\n> `disabled: true` ov"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"erride into the profile's `cordis.patch.yml` (the user\n> config layer). dsh watches that file (`watc"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"hUserPatches`), so the change\n> applies live without a restart, survives restarts, and deleting the "},{"id":"p18s4","text":"row\n> restores the default.\n>\n> **Why the raw id (fixed in v0.4)**: loader entries carry a path-pref"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"ixed full\n> id (`include:ssh`), but the patch layer matches each config row's own `id`\n> field (`ssh"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"`). Older versions wrote the prefixed id into the patch file, so\n> the row was skipped at boot (\"pat"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"ch: entry not found\") and the toggle was\n> silently lost on restart. v0.4 writes the raw id, keeps t"},{"id":"p18s8","text":"he full id for\n> `ctx.loader.update`, and cleans up legacy `include:<id>` rows."},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Origin is derived from the package scope by default; edge cases (e.g. a\nthird-party package publishe"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"d under `@deepseek-ai/`) are overridden via\n`extraUserPackages`. Override this plugin's row in the p"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"rofile's\n`cordis.patch.yml`:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Repository layout"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"## Docs"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- DESIGN.md — design rationale and source evidence (why a new tab\ninstead of modifying the official "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"one; classification rules and edge cases)"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Related"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"- deepseek-harness — DeepSeek Harness official repo (DSH itself)\n- omdsh-dev/community — community p"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"lugin submissions & collaboration hub"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"MIT · Copyright (c) 2025 tttwh"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
